 "structural_change": "STRUCTURAL qkd_kvs_ctl_s32a (KV-CTL3 10-20, successor of qkd_kvs_ctl_mu6c: PRE-GATE NATIVE CENSUS FAIL on the mu6c/d mapped netlist, max driver 2357 loads, 125 drivers > 32, d39dbc577 / results/arch/kv_ctl3_1020/viol.txt). Real RTL successors (generator tools/qwen_kv_die/gen_kvs_ctl_s32.py; shared originals byte-identical): writer + writer programme (kept slot/index copy families, 2-level, no added edge), fan root (35 ph1 copies, early use_b family), layer programme (every held register in <=16-b slices behind kept-hierarchy ot_s32_sel/ot_s32_and leaves with per-slice kept literals; fault split family), boot dispatcher (per-target accepts, sliced data, one-hot strobe group leaves), die cfg (kept field leaves + explicit POR copies), ownership calendar (sliced root banks). Same ports, same geometry/macros/pins/clock as the predecessor; 0 added edges; outputs identical on every edge (module lockstep benches + the real-boot MU tile bench).",
